     1	"""Production background loops: the boundary tick every tick_seconds via
     2	asyncio.to_thread, and — replacing the removed dispatcher loop — System A, the readiness
     3	poll that drives System B. An iteration's exception is logged and never kills the loop.
     4	Test mode never starts these; that gating lives in the lifespan (core/server.py), so this
     5	module stays directly callable for tests.
     6	
     7	System A runs on its own daemon thread (its fast-path poke is a threading.Event, not an
     8	asyncio sleep to interrupt). It is guarded by the master switch (config.dispatch_enabled —
     9	W3a delegated: System A reuses it) and the relocated machine-wide lock
    10	(runtime.lock.ensure_machine_lock), so only one poller drives the board per machine. System
    11	B is constructed with the planner home + Hermes interpreter from config; its real gateway
    12	spawn is only ever reachable here (outside test mode), so ./verify stays hermetic."""
