     1	"""Ticket routes (§9), plus the ticket-anchored links and the ticket-centric
     2	derived views (board, queues). Thin HTTP shells over the stage-3 writers and the
     3	pure read views: every handler is parse -> auth -> writer -> serialize. No route
     4	re-implements a domain rule and no route appends events.
     5	
     6	This module also homes the shared request plumbing (config/clock accessors, the
     7	per-request connection dependency, the transaction context manager, and the enum
     8	and body-key marshallers). The other api modules import these from here; the direction
     9	is strictly one-way (sprints/days/dispatch api -> tickets api), and views modules
    10	import no api module at all.
    11	
    12	Request bodies arrive as plain dicts and are marshalled into the TypedDict shapes
    13	declared in each domain's contracts (§14); a null or wrong-typed key raises the
    14	validation envelope rather than FastAPI's 422, so the CLI and UI see one error shape."""
    15	
