orchestration/tickets/W3b-systema-gate-cli/plan-review.out:6814:  `plan.md:72-75` defines `SystemA.poke(self) -> None`, but `plan.md:112-117` makes `MindQueue.on_idle` call with `key`, and `plan.md:135` wires `system_b.set_idle_callback(system_a.poke)`. The current System B shape confirms the trap: `src/planner/runtime/system_b.py:91-100` stores a `Callable[[str], None]` and calls it with `ticket_id`. That will either fail mypy or log a runtime `TypeError`, so step-completion fast path will not fire.
orchestration/tickets/W3b-systema-gate-cli/plan-review.out:6815:  Minimal fix: make System B’s stored idle callback zero-arg and ignore the key, or wire `lambda _key: system_a.poke()` with matching types.
orchestration/tickets/W3b-systema-gate-cli/plan-review.out:6818:  `plan.md:51-54` does `_is_ready` then `set_off`; `plan.md:93-98` only closes the duplicate enqueue window with `has_inflight`. But `src/planner/runtime/system_b.py:136-139` unconditionally writes `agent_working` when the queued item starts. If a human drops the ticket, changes grant to `at_cap=stop`, parks a proposal, or adds a blocking link after System A’s read but before the queue worker starts, System B still runs a stale prompt.
orchestration/tickets/W3b-systema-gate-cli/plan-review.out:6832:Hermetic test safety is sound if implemented as planned: `create_app` skips background loops under `config.test_mode` (`src/planner/core/server.py:89-97`), and e2e `plan serve` sets `PLAN_TEST_MODE=1` (`tests/e2e/conftest.py:81-92`). The API `system_a` null-guard plan is the right shape.
orchestration/tickets/W3b-systema-gate-cli/plan-review.out:6842:  `plan.md:72-75` defines `SystemA.poke(self) -> None`, but `plan.md:112-117` makes `MindQueue.on_idle` call with `key`, and `plan.md:135` wires `system_b.set_idle_callback(system_a.poke)`. The current System B shape confirms the trap: `src/planner/runtime/system_b.py:91-100` stores a `Callable[[str], None]` and calls it with `ticket_id`. That will either fail mypy or log a runtime `TypeError`, so step-completion fast path will not fire.
orchestration/tickets/W3b-systema-gate-cli/plan-review.out:6843:  Minimal fix: make System B’s stored idle callback zero-arg and ignore the key, or wire `lambda _key: system_a.poke()` with matching types.
orchestration/tickets/W3b-systema-gate-cli/plan-review.out:6846:  `plan.md:51-54` does `_is_ready` then `set_off`; `plan.md:93-98` only closes the duplicate enqueue window with `has_inflight`. But `src/planner/runtime/system_b.py:136-139` unconditionally writes `agent_working` when the queued item starts. If a human drops the ticket, changes grant to `at_cap=stop`, parks a proposal, or adds a blocking link after System A’s read but before the queue worker starts, System B still runs a stale prompt.
