codex
No blockers found. One should-fix concurrency gap and one nit/test gap.

**Findings**

**should-fix** [src/planner/runtime/system_b.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/runtime/system_b.py:159): the F2 stale-set-off guard is present, but not atomic with the `agent_working` start write. `_run()` checks `guard(...)` at line 159, then calls `tickets_data.set_run_status(...)` at lines 163-165; that helper opens its own `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` later in [src/planner/tickets/data.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/tickets/data.py:206). A human drop/grant-stop/block/park committed in that tiny gap can still lead to a stale `agent_working` write and spawn. Minimal fix: perform the guard read and start-status write inside one immediate transaction, likely via a guarded start helper in `tickets_data` so the single status-write door stays intact.

**nit** [tests/e2e/test_cli_verbs.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/tests/e2e/test_cli_verbs.py:33): the comment says `--date` is tested, but lines 34-35 only run an unscoped `ticket list`. The implementation has `--date`; the test just does not exercise it. Minimal fix: add `ticket list --date 2026-07-04` and assert it matches the `--day today` filtered set under the fake clock.

**Sound Axes**

F1 landed: `SystemA.poke(self, _key: str | None = None)` accepts both the idle callback’s ticket id and arg-less API pokes at [system_a.py:74](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/runtime/system_a.py:74). No remaining TypeError path in the direct `set_idle_callback(system_a.poke)` wiring at [loops.py:108](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/core/loops.py:108).

F2 mostly landed: `guard` defaults to `None` at [system_b.py:88](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/runtime/system_b.py:88), System A passes `readiness.is_runnable` at [system_a.py:99](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/runtime/system_a.py:99), and skips write/spawn when false at [system_b.py:159](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/runtime/system_b.py:159). `readiness.is_runnable` correctly contains no `has_inflight` at [readiness.py:19](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/runtime/readiness.py:19). The remaining issue is the non-atomic gap above.

F3 landed: `POST /tickets` pokes System A after creation at [tickets/api.py:246](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/tickets/api.py:246) and [tickets/api.py:267](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/tickets/api.py:267).

F4 landed: candidate SQL is candidate-only by status and terminal state, excluding `agent_working` and `errored`, at [system_a.py:33](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/runtime/system_a.py:33).

Readiness semantics are sound: terminal, no gating for `needs_review`, parked proposal, `at_cap=stop` at/beyond ceiling, and blocked checks match `machine`, `admission`, and `resolution` at [readiness.py:25](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/runtime/readiness.py:25). System A does not write `tickets.status`; status writes remain in System B via `tickets_data.set_run_status`.

Fast path is sound: `MindQueue` clears `_active` and notifies before calling `on_idle` outside the lock at [queue.py:81](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/minds/queue.py:81). `has_inflight` delegates to synchronized `is_active` at [system_b.py:97](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/runtime/system_b.py:97). I do not see a deadlock, double-fire bug, or correctness lost-wake in `SystemA._run_loop`.

Hermetic safety is sound: server lifespan skips loops in test mode at [server.py:89](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/core/server.py:89); real `spawn_popen` is wired only from [loops.py:100](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/core/loops.py:100); e2e sets `PLAN_TEST_MODE=1` at [tests/e2e/conftest.py:84](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/tests/e2e/conftest.py:84). API pokes are null-guarded through `_poke` at [tickets/api.py:105](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/tickets/api.py:105).

Server wiring and CLI/day-filter changes are otherwise sound. No active dangling `pickup` references in `src`, `tests`, `assets`, or `static`; remaining hits are review artifacts. Import smoke for `planner.tickets.api`, `planner.core.server`, and `planner.runtime.system_a` passed.

Checks: `ruff check src tests --no-cache` passed; `git diff --check` passed. `ruff check . --no-cache` fails on pre-existing orchestration smoke import ordering, outside the W3b implementation. `mypy --no-incremental` could not run in this read-only sandbox because mypy 2.1.0 still tried to open its SQLite cache.

Verdict: **APPROVE-WITH-FIXES**.
